  VOLUME AND SPEAKER ONLY. A turn using the word "brace" is not a catch, and this scanner
  cannot tell them apart — so nothing here says who caught anything. `credited→keeper` counts
  committee turns that credit the human ("you caught…", "you're right that…"); it is a phrase
  count, not a keeper-caught tally.

  THE MATURITY RATIO USED TO BE PRINTED HERE AND WAS DELETED (2026-07-28, chair decision).
  It scored by SPEAKER and called the result CATCHER. When catch-ledger.js's withholding rule
  was applied to it honestly it withheld 15 of 16 windows and the survivor read 0:1 — the
  instrument reporting that it could not compute what it named. `catch-ledger.js` computes it
  over the curated prose record, where attribution is actually written down, and is now the
  room's only computation of it. Quote that one; do not reconstruct this one from these
  columns, which is the move the deletion exists to prevent.

These are candidates. Nothing here is a verdict about a pane or a person — read the lines
(--show <tell>) and judge them. A falling rate is not progress; it is also what learning
which phrases are counted looks like.
